IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part IV, "Rulings and Appeals": sections 90 to 94.
-- Who may ask the Canada Revenue Agency for a ruling and about what, by when, what a ruling settles when none is asked
-- for, the appeal to the Minister from a ruling or an assessment, and how the Minister must handle an appeal.
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Unofficial plain-text source; nothing verified
-- against the official text.
--
-- Time limits follow the keel's reading (fork F4, and F-ei3-18 below): "within 90 days after" a day ends on that day PLUS 90 and
-- that last day counts; "before the June 30 following the year" means strictly before 30 June.
-- A judgment the Act leaves to the Minister or an officer ("reasonable time", "adequate" manner) is a BOOLEAN input.

§ `Section 90 - rulings`

DECLARE `ei3 Person who asks for a ruling` IS ONE OF
    `ei3 an employer`
    `ei3 an employee`
    `ei3 a person claiming to be an employer`
    `ei3 a person claiming to be an employee`
    `ei3 the Commission`
    `ei3 someone not named in subsection 90(1)`

-- The nine questions of s 90(1)(a) to (i); the last constructor is the explicit "not on the list".
DECLARE `ei3 Question for a ruling` IS ONE OF
    `ei3 whether an employment is insurable`
    `ei3 how long an insurable employment lasts, including the dates on which it begins and ends`
    `ei3 what is the amount of any insurable earnings`
    `ei3 how many hours an insured person has had in insurable employment`
    `ei3 whether a premium is payable`
    `ei3 what is the amount of a premium payable`
    `ei3 who is the employer of an insured person`
    `ei3 whether employers are associated employers`
    `ei3 what amount shall be refunded under subsections 96(4) to (10)`
    `ei3 a question not named in subsection 90(1)`

-- src:1456 | 90 (1) An employer, an employee, a person claiming to be an employer or an employee or the Commission may request an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency authorized by the Minister to make a ruling on any of the following questions:
-- src:1457 | (a) whether an employment is insurable;
-- src:1458 | (b) how long an insurable employment lasts, including the dates on which it begins and ends;
-- src:1459 | (c) what is the amount of any insurable earnings;
-- src:1460 | (d) how many hours an insured person has had in insurable employment;
-- src:1461 | (e) whether a premium is payable;
-- src:1462 | (f) what is the amount of a premium payable;
-- src:1463 | (g) who is the employer of an insured person;
-- src:1464 | (h) whether employers are associated employers; and
-- src:1465 | (i) what amount shall be refunded under subsections 96(4) to (10).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 90(1)(a) to (i) (src:1456-1465)
GIVEN question IS A `ei3 Question for a ruling`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` IS
    CONSIDER question
    WHEN `ei3 a question not named in subsection 90(1)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Who may ask which questions. A listed person asking a listed question: JUST TRUE. The text lists those who "may request"; it does not
-- say that no one else may, so for anyone else, or any other question, the answer is NOTHING (fork F-ei3-18).
-- src:1456 | 90 (1) An employer, an employee, a person claiming to be an employer or an employee or the Commission may request an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency authorized by the Minister to make a ruling on any of the following questions:
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 90(1) (src:1456)
GIVEN requester IS A `ei3 Person who asks for a ruling`
      question IS A `ei3 Question for a ruling`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 90(1) the person may request a ruling of an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency on the question` IS
    CONSIDER requester
    WHEN `ei3 someone not named in subsection 90(1)` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` question THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (2): the Commission at any time; anyone else "before the June 30 following the year to which the question relates".
-- "Before" is read strictly: a request made on 30 June is too late (fork F-ei3-18).
-- src:1467 | (2) The Commission may request a ruling at any time, but a request by any other person must be made before the June 30 following the year to which the question relates.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 90(2) (src:1467)
GIVEN `the request is made by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year to which the question relates` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the request is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 90(2) the request for a ruling is made in time` IF
        `the request is made by the Commission`
    OR  `the day on which the request is made` LESS THAN (YMD (`the year to which the question relates` PLUS 1) 6 30)

-- Subsection (3): "within a reasonable time after receiving the request" is the officer's judgment call.
-- src:1469 | (3) The authorized officer shall make the ruling within a reasonable time after receiving the request.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 90(3) (src:1469)
GIVEN `the authorized officer has made the ruling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time taken after receiving the request is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 90(3) the authorized officer has made the ruling within a reasonable time` IF
        `the authorized officer has made the ruling`
    AND `the time taken after receiving the request is a reasonable time`

-- Subsection (4): "Unless a ruling has been requested with respect to an insured person": (a) an amount deducted or paid as a
-- premium for the person is deemed to have been deducted or paid in accordance with the Act; (b) an amount not deducted or paid
-- is deemed not to have been required to be.
-- src:1471 | (4) Unless a ruling has been requested with respect to an insured person,
-- src:1472 | (a) an amount deducted from the remuneration of the person or paid by an employer as a premium for the person is deemed to have been deducted or paid in accordance with this Act; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 90(4)(a) (src:1471-1472)
GIVEN `a ruling has been requested with respect to the insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount was deducted from the remuneration of the person or paid by an employer as a premium for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 90(4)(a) the amount is deemed to have been deducted or paid in accordance with this Act` IF
        (NOT `a ruling has been requested with respect to the insured person`)
    AND `the amount was deducted from the remuneration of the person or paid by an employer as a premium for the person`

-- src:1471 | (4) Unless a ruling has been requested with respect to an insured person,
-- src:1472 | (a) an amount deducted from the remuneration of the person or paid by an employer as a premium for the person is deemed to have been deducted or paid in accordance with this Act; or
-- src:1473 | (b) an amount that has not been so deducted or paid is deemed not to have been required to be deducted or paid in accordance with this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 90(4)(b) (src:1471) (src:1473)
GIVEN `a ruling has been requested with respect to the insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount has not been so deducted or paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 90(4)(b) the amount is deemed not to have been required to be deducted or paid in accordance with this Act` IF
        (NOT `a ruling has been requested with respect to the insured person`)
    AND `the amount has not been so deducted or paid`

-- src:1475 | 90.1 If a question specified in section 90 arises in the consideration of a claim for benefits, a ruling must be made by an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, as set out in that section.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 90.1 (src:1475)
GIVEN question IS A `ei3 Question for a ruling`
      `the question arises in the consideration of a claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 90.1 a ruling must be made by an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IF
        `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` question
    AND `the question arises in the consideration of a claim for benefits`

§ `Sections 91 to 94 - appeals`

-- Section 91: the Commission "at any time"; any other person concerned "within 90 days after the person is notified of the ruling".
-- src:1477 | 91 An appeal to the Minister from a ruling may be made by the Commission at any time and by any other person concerned within 90 days after the person is notified of the ruling.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 91 (src:1477)
GIVEN `the appellant is the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant is another person concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person was notified of the ruling` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the appeal to the Minister is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 91 the appeal to the Minister from the ruling is made in time` IF
        `the appellant is the Commission`
    OR (    `the appellant is another person concerned`
        AND `the day on which the appeal to the Minister is made` AT MOST (`the last day of` 90 `days after` `the day on which the person was notified of the ruling`))

-- Section 92: an employer assessed under section 85 may appeal for a reconsideration "either as to whether an amount should be
-- assessed as payable or as to the amount assessed", within 90 days after being notified of the assessment.
-- src:1479 | 92 An employer who has been assessed under section 85 may appeal to the Minister for a reconsideration of the assessment, either as to whether an amount should be assessed as payable or as to the amount assessed, within 90 days after being notified of the assessment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 92 (src:1479)
GIVEN `the employer has been assessed under section 85` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the employer was notified of the assessment` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the appeal to the Minister is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 92 the employer may appeal to the Minister for a reconsideration of the assessment` IF
        `the employer has been assessed under section 85`
    AND `the day on which the appeal to the Minister is made` AT MOST (`the last day of` 90 `days after` `the day on which the employer was notified of the assessment`)

-- Section 93(1): the Minister shall notify any person who may be affected by an appeal (the Commission, on an appeal of a
-- ruling) of the intention to decide it, and give them an opportunity to provide information and make representations to
-- protect their interests, "as the circumstances require".
-- src:1481 | 93 (1) The Minister shall notify any person who may be affected by an appeal of the Minister’s intention to decide the appeal, including the Commission in the case of an appeal of a ruling, and shall give them an opportunity to provide information and to make representations to protect their interests, as the circumstances require.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 93(1) (src:1481)
GIVEN `the person may be affected by the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Commission and the appeal is an appeal of a ruling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 93(1) the person is to be notified of the Minister's intention to decide the appeal and heard` IF
        `the person may be affected by the appeal`
    OR  `the person is the Commission and the appeal is an appeal of a ruling`

-- src:1481 | 93 (1) The Minister shall notify any person who may be affected by an appeal of the Minister’s intention to decide the appeal, including the Commission in the case of an appeal of a ruling, and shall give them an opportunity to provide information and to make representations to protect their interests, as the circumstances require.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 93(1) (src:1481)
GIVEN `the person is to be notified and heard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister notified the person of the intention to decide the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister gave the person an opportunity to provide information and to make representations to protect their interests, as the circumstances require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 93(1) the Minister has done what the subsection requires` IF
        (NOT `the person is to be notified and heard`)
    OR  (`the Minister notified the person of the intention to decide the appeal` AND `the Minister gave the person an opportunity to provide information and to make representations to protect their interests, as the circumstances require`)

-- src:1483 | (2) An appeal shall be addressed to the Assistant Director of Appeals in a Tax Services Office of the Canada Revenue Agency and delivered or mailed to that office.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 93(2) (src:1483)
GIVEN `the appeal is addressed to the Assistant Director of Appeals in a Tax Services Office of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is delivered or mailed to that office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 93(2) the appeal has been sent as required` IF
        `the appeal is addressed to the Assistant Director of Appeals in a Tax Services Office of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    AND `it is delivered or mailed to that office`

-- src:1485 | (3) The Minister shall decide the appeal within a reasonable time after receiving it and shall notify the affected persons of the decision.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 93(3) (src:1485)
GIVEN `the Minister decided the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time taken after receiving it is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister notified the affected persons of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 93(3) the Minister has decided the appeal and notified the affected persons as required` IF
        `the Minister decided the appeal`
    AND `the time taken after receiving it is a reasonable time`
    AND `the Minister notified the affected persons of the decision`

-- src:1487 | (4) If the Minister is required to notify a person who may be or is affected by an appeal, the Minister may have the person notified in such manner as the Minister considers adequate.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 93(4) (src:1487)
GIVEN `the Minister is required to notify a person who may be or is affected by an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister considers the manner of notification adequate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 93(4) the Minister may have the person notified in that manner` IF
        `the Minister is required to notify a person who may be or is affected by an appeal`
    AND `the Minister considers the manner of notification adequate`

-- Section 94: sections 90 to 93 do NOT restrict the Minister's authority to decide under this Part or Part VII on the Minister's
-- own initiative, or to assess after the date in s 90(2). For anything else the section says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:1489 | 94 Nothing in sections 90 to 93 restricts the authority of the Minister to make a decision under this Part or Part VII on the Minister’s own initiative or to make an assessment after the date mentioned in subsection 90(2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 94 (src:1489)
GIVEN `the authority is to make a decision under this Part or Part VII on the Minister's own initiative, or to make an assessment after the date mentioned in subsection 90(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 94 sections 90 to 93 restrict the Minister's authority` IS
    IF `the authority is to make a decision under this Part or Part VII on the Minister's own initiative, or to make an assessment after the date mentioned in subsection 90(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
